-- title:
--   Directed supersingular-fibre dictionary under Γ₀(M')-level automorphisms
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $q$, a natural number $M'$ with $q \nmid M'$, and a prime $\ell_g$ with $\ell_g \equiv 11 \pmod{12}$, $\ell_g \mid M'$ and $\ell_g \in M'.\mathrm{primeFactors}$ (the last two recorded separately as `hℓgM'` and `hℓgpf`).
--
--   **Reduction data at $q$.** Let $A$ be a valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbb Q} =$ `AlgebraicClosure ℚ` with `A.LiesOverPrime q`, i.e. $q$ lies in the non-units of $A$. Let $W$ be a finite set of places of `modularFunctionFieldC (ResidueField A) M'` over `ResidueField A`, and `hW` the requirement that $W$ consist exactly of the members of `ssPlaces q M' (ResidueField A)`, the places satisfying `IsSupersingularPlace q M' _`. The hypothesis `hle` asserts `modularFunctionFieldBar M' ≤ fieldBar q M'`, i.e. the base change to $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ of the full level-$M'$ modular function field sits inside the level-$q^2M'$ field attached to `levelH q M'`. Let $R_0$ be a `ConstantReduction` for $A$ from $\overline{\mathbb Q}$-Laurent-series field `modularFunctionFieldBar M'` to `modularFunctionFieldC (ResidueField A) M'`: that is, a valuation subring $R_0.\mathrm{integers}$, a surjective residue homomorphism onto the target with kernel the maximal ideal, a map on places preserving degrees and compatible with divisor push-forward, containing the constants $A$ with the expected residues, and satisfying the rescaling property `exists_smul_mem`. The hypothesis `hR₀` says that $R_0$ computes coefficientwise reduction: for every Laurent series $y$ over $A$ whose image under `coeffMap A.subtype` lies in `modularFunctionFieldBar M'`, that image lies in $R_0.\mathrm{integers}$ and its $R_0$-residue is, as a Laurent series over `ResidueField A`, the coefficientwise reduction of $y$. Finally $s$ is a chosen element of $W$, i.e. a supersingular place of the level-$M'$ fibre field.
--
--   **Small constants.** Let $k_0$ be an intermediate field of $\mathbb Q \subseteq \overline{\mathbb Q}$ and $\pi_0 \in k_0$ an element lying in $A$, and put $A_0 := A.\mathrm{comap}(k_0 \to \overline{\mathbb Q})$, the valuation ring $A \cap k_0$. The hypotheses `hdvr`, `hunif`, `hhens`, `hres` require $A_0$ to be a discrete valuation ring with maximal ideal generated by $\pi_0$, henselian local, and with algebraically closed residue field $\kappa :=$ `ResidueField A₀`; `hκ` requires every element of $A$ to be congruent, modulo the maximal ideal of $A$, to an element of $k_0 \cap A$.
--
--   **Roots of unity and the rigid field.** Let $\xi \in k_0$ be a primitive $q$-th root of unity (`hξ`) admitting a ring homomorphism $\iota : k_0 \to \mathbb C$ with $\iota\xi = e^{2\pi i/q}$ (`hιξ`). Let $H_1 \le (\mathbb Z/q^2M')^\times$ be given by `hH₁` as the intersection of `levelH q M'` (the kernel of reduction to $(\mathbb Z/q)^\times$) with the kernel of reduction to $(\mathbb Z/\ell_g)^\times$. Let $K$ be the intermediate field of $k_0 \subseteq$ `LaurentSeries k₀` given by `hK` as `laurentBaseChange k₀ (xHFunctionField (q ^ 2 * M') H₁)`, equipped with an $A_0$-algebra structure compatible with $k_0$, and let $j \in K$ have underlying Laurent series `coeffEmb k₀ jq`, with $j \neq 0$. Write $C :=$ `TwoChartIntegralModel.chartAlgFin A₀ K j` for the associated chart subalgebra of $K$ over $A_0$, and let
--   $$Y := \{\, y \subseteq C \text{ an ideal} \ \mid\ y \text{ maximal and the image of } \pi_0 \text{ in } C \text{ lies in } y \,\}$$
--   be the set of closed points of the special fibre of that chart.
--
--   **Moduli-theoretic input.** The hypotheses `hℓ` and `hM` state, for all $A_0$-algebras $T$, that `IsGamma1Point W ℓg D` is preserved under variable change (with $D$ replaced by `D.variableChange C`) and that `IsGamma0PowAt W p k h` is preserved under variable change (with $h$ replaced by `kernelVariableChangeDeg C (gamma0PowDeg p k) h`). Let $\mathcal G$ be a family of relative group laws `GroupLaws A₀`, chord-and-tangent (`h𝒢`) and with the origin as identity (`h𝒢O`), and $\mathcal T$ a `LevelTransport A₀ 𝒢 q` which is a section transport (`h𝒯`). The hypotheses `hVC` and `hCO` provide, for every $A_0$-algebra and every variable change, respectively every $A_0$-algebra map, a graded ring homomorphism between the projective-model graded rings with the irrelevant-ideal bound and satisfying `IsVariableChangeHom`, respectively `IsCoefficientHom`. Write $R :=$ `rigidDataGamma1Pow A₀ ℓg M' q hℓ hM 𝒢 𝒯`, the rigid Weierstrass data obtained from the product of the $\Gamma_0$-power component at $M'$, the $\Gamma_1(\ell_g)$ component and the level-$q$ Drinfeld component; for a raw structure $x$ over $\kappa$, $x.\mathrm{curve}$ is a Weierstrass curve with unit discriminant, $x.\mathrm{level}.1$ is the $\Gamma_0$-power datum (a family of polynomials indexed by the prime factors of $M'$), $x.\mathrm{level}.2.1$ is a `LevelPData` $(x_P,y_P,x_Q,y_Q)$ and $x.\mathrm{level}.2.2$ a `RawDrinfeldPair`. Points of the associated moduli set are the classes in $R.\mathrm{Pt}\,\kappa$, the quotient of raw structures by $R.\mathrm{Rel}$, and $R.\mathrm{act}\,C_0$ is the action of a variable change on raw structures.
--
--   **Conclusion.** There exists a map $\Phi$ from $Y$ to the raw $R$-structures over $\kappa$ with the following five properties. Throughout, say that $y \in Y$ *lies over $s$* when the following holds: for every Laurent series $g$ over $\mathbb Q$ belonging to `modularFunctionFieldFull M'` whose image in `modularFunctionFieldBar M'` lies in $R_0.\mathrm{integers}$, such that $g$ has non-negative order (in the sense of `Place.ord`) at every place of `modularFunctionFieldBar M'` over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ at which `jq` has non-negative order, and such that the $R_0$-residue of $g$ lies in the valuation subring of the place $s$; and for every witness that `coeffEmb k₀ g` lies in $K$ and that the resulting element of $K$ lies in $C$; and for every $c \in k_0$ with $c \in A$ whose residue in `ResidueField A` equals $s.\mathrm{evalAt}$ of the $R_0$-residue of $g$ — the difference in $C$ between that element and the image of $c$ under $A_0 \to C$ lies in $y$.
--
--   (i) For every $y \in Y$ there are $x_G, y_G \in \kappa$ such that $(x_G,y_G)$ satisfies the affine equation of $(\Phi y).\mathrm{curve}$, the polynomial of the $\Gamma_0$-power datum $(\Phi y).\mathrm{level}.1$ at the prime factor $\ell_g$ of $M'$ vanishes at $x_G$, and, as points of the base change of $(\Phi y).\mathrm{curve}$ to $\kappa$ formed by `LevelRelabelling.toPoint`, the $\Gamma_1$-point $(x_P,y_P)$ of $(\Phi y).\mathrm{level}.2.1$ equals $\ell_g^{\,v-1}$ times the point $(x_G,y_G)$, where $v = M'.\mathrm{factorization}\,\ell_g$.
--
--   (ii) For every $y \in Y$ lying over $s$: every point $P$ of the affine curve $(\Phi y).\mathrm{curve}$ with $q \cdot P = 0$ is zero.
--
--   (iii) For all $y, y' \in Y$, each lying over $s$, there is a variable change $C_0$ over $\kappa$ such that $R.\mathrm{act}\,C_0\,(\Phi y)$ has the same curve and the same $\Gamma_0$-power datum as $\Phi y'$, and such that `InLine ((Φ y').curve) ℓg` holds for the pair consisting of the $x_P$ of $(\Phi y').\mathrm{level}.2.1$ and the $x_P$ of the level datum of $R.\mathrm{act}\,C_0\,(\Phi y)$, i.e. there is $a$ with $1 \le a \le (\ell_g-1)/2$ and $x \cdot (\Psi^2_a)(x_0) = \Phi_a(x_0)$ for these two $x$-coordinates.
--
--   (iv) (Directed relabelling.) For every $\gamma \in SL_2(\mathbb Z)$ lying in $\Gamma_0(M')$, every $\tau : K \simeq_{k_0} K$ with `IsLevelAutAt k₀ q ξ q (q ^ 2 * M') H₁ γ K τ` — so that $\tau$ realises, on ratios of weight-$k$ modular forms for $\Gamma_{H_1}(q^2M')$ with integral $q$-expansions, the slash action of the level-$q$ conjugate `conjElemN q γ`, read through any embedding $k_0 \to \mathbb C$ sending $\xi$ to $e^{2\pi i/q}$ — such that $\tau$ maps $C$ into $C$, and all $y, y_1 \in Y$ such that for every $b \in C$ with $\tau b \in C$ one has $b \in y$ if and only if $\tau b \in y_1$: for all raw structures $x, x_1$ over $\kappa$ and every proof $h_\Delta$ that the discriminant of $x.\mathrm{level}.2.2.\mathrm{curve}$ is a unit, if the class of $x$ in $R.\mathrm{Pt}\,\kappa$ equals the class of $\Phi y$, if $x_1.\mathrm{curve} = x.\mathrm{curve}$ and $x_1.\mathrm{level}.1 = x.\mathrm{level}.1$, if the point of $x_1.\mathrm{level}.2.1$ on the base change of $x.\mathrm{curve}$ to $\kappa$ equals $\gamma_{00}$ times the corresponding point of $x.\mathrm{level}.2.1$ (where $\gamma_{00}$ is the upper-left entry of $\gamma$), if $x_1.\mathrm{level}.2.1$ satisfies $x_Q = x_P$ and $y_Q = y_P$, and if $x_1.\mathrm{level}.2.2 =$ `RawDrinfeldPair.relabel 𝒢 γ x.level.2.2 hΔ` (the Drinfeld pair obtained by the $\mathbb Z$-linear combination of $P,Q$ with the columns of $\gamma$), then the class of $\Phi y_1$ in $R.\mathrm{Pt}\,\kappa$ equals the class of $x_1$.
--
--   (v) (Injectivity on classes.) For all $y, y' \in Y$ such that $y'$ lies over $s$, if the classes of $\Phi y$ and $\Phi y'$ in $R.\mathrm{Pt}\,\kappa$ coincide, then $y = y'$. Only $y'$ is required to lie over $s$ here.
--
--   This is the $\Gamma_0(M')$-equivariant ("directed") form of the dictionary between the closed points of the special fibre of the integral chart of the level-$H_1$ modular curve at a supersingular place and the raw diamond-rigid Weierstrass data with $\Gamma_0(M')$-, $\Gamma_1(\ell_g)$- and Drinfeld level-$q$ structure over the algebraically closed residue field: clause (iv) states that a level automorphism attached to $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$ moves the class of a point by the relabelling of the level structure by $\gamma$, with no congruence condition on $\gamma$ modulo $q$. It is used in the analysis of the diamond operators on the supersingular fibre, in particular by [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.Diamond.levelAut_sub_self_mem_of_isLevelAutAt_of_mem_gamma0_of_apply_eq_one_of_over_ssPlace_rigidDataGamma1Pow`](thm.html#ModularCurve.FullLevel.Diamond.levelAut_sub_self_mem_of_isLevelAutAt_of_mem_gamma0_of_apply_eq_one_of_over_ssPlace_rigidDataGamma1Pow).
